# Template: rule (rule_kind decision). It names its capability because only
# this capability uses it; a rule used by several capabilities is shared.
# Required: ready, kind, id, rule_kind, title, summary, and the logic for its kind:
#   decision: when / then / otherwise, a decision graph {nodes, edges}, a table
#     {columns, rows}, or a judge {evidence, output, gate, prompt}; optional
#     default, precedence, inputs, params, calculations, sets.
#   invariant: holds, scope.   policy: whenever, then, sequence.
#   quality: applies_to, measure, target, scope.
# Optional: capability, rules (rules this rule applies), constants,
#   constraints [{text, hard}].
# A decision or policy rule must be applied through the rules field of a
# step, an edge, a sequence message, or another rule; a policy also by its
# own sequence.
ready: 2
kind: rule
id: notes.note-length
display_id: RULE-NOTE-LENGTH
rule_kind: decision
capability: notes
title: A note fits the length limit
summary: A note longer than the limit is refused and the person keeps their text.
when: The note's text is longer than the length limit
then: The save is refused as too long and the editor keeps the text
otherwise: The note is saved
constants:
  - constant.max-length
